    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀει-πάρθενος</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ever a virgin</i>, 
			<i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				96
			</span></i> (in 
				Aeol.
			form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀϊπ-</span>); of the
			Vestals, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱἱέρειαι αἱ ἀειπ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					56.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				59.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> language, of the number <i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i> (as being neither factor nor multiple of any number up to
				<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.46
			</span></i>; of the Sabbath, ib.<i><span class="en">
				497
			</span></i>.</div>
